<USER_REQUEST>
Calculate the entropy change (J/mol K) of the given reaction. The molar entropies [J/K mol] are given in brackets after each substance.

\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} [91.2] + 3 \text{O}_2(g) [205.1] \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} [66.5] + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) [248.2] \]
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the entropy change (ΔS) for the given reaction, we use the formula:

\[
\Delta S = \sum (\text{Osm}_2 \times \text{Osm}_i) - \sum (\text{OSO}_1 \times \text{OsO}_1)
\]

Where:
- \( \text{Osm}_2 \) is the osmotic coefficient of the final reactants.
- \( \text{OsO}_1 \) is the osmotic coefficient of the initial reactants.

For the given reaction:

\[
2 \text{PbS(s)} + 3 \text{O}_2(g) \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} + 2 \text{SO}_2(g)
\]

The molar isomities are:
- \( \text{PbS(s)} = 91.2 \, \text{J/K \cdot \text{mol}} \)
- \( \text{O}_2(g) = 205.1 \, \text{J/K \cdot \text{mol}} \)
- \( \text{PbO(s)} = 66.5 \, \text{J/K \cdot \text{mol}} \)
- \( \text{SO}_2(g) = 248.2 \, \text{J/K \cdot \text{mol}} \)

Substituting these values into the formula:

\[
\Delta S = (2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2) - (2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1)
\]

\[
\Delta S = (133 + 496.4) - (182.4 + 615.3)
\]

\[
\Delta S = 629.4 - 797.7
\]

\[
\Delta S = -168.3 \, \text{J/K \cdot \text{mol}}
\]

The entropy change for the reaction is \(\boxed{-168.3 \, \text{J/K \cdot \text{mol}}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

