   Since \( B \setminus A \subseteq A \), it implies \( B \setminus A \subseteq A \).  
   The set \( B \setminus A \) contains all elements in \( B \) that are not in \( A \).  
   If \( B \setminus A \) is a subset of \( A \), it means no element in \( B \) is not in \( A \).  
   Therefore, every element in \( B \) must also be in \( A \), proving \( B \subseteq A \).  

