For $n=1$, we have $a_{1}=1$.

For $n\geqslant 2$, we have $a_{1}+2a_{2}+4a_{3}+…+{2}^{n-2}{a}_{n-1}+{2}^{n-1}{a}_{n}=2n-1$.

Subtracting the previous equation from this, we get $2^{n-1}{a}_{n}=2n-1-(2n-2)=1$.

Therefore, $a_{n}= \frac{1}{2^{n-1}}$ for $n\geqslant 1$.

Now, we can find the sum of the first $n$ terms of the sequence ${{S}_{n}}$:

